Subject: Cantor EVO-X2 Needle 2 SOP Attention Runtime

Description: Bounded implementation authority for an effectless experimental sidecar on EVO-X2 in which Needle 2 selects content-addressed attention procedures, the host verifies and executes registered pure contracts, Cantor supplies proof-carrying SOP query results, and the existing unmodified llama.cpp server articulates a final response from the admitted frame.

@ [specification_uuid] a0641b62-f964-46b8-ad29-6a79d557ecff
@ [profile] cantor-evox2-needle-attention-runtime/0.1
@ [source_manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-18_evox2_needle2_sop_attention_runtime\Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [base_query] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_SOP_Query_Microkernel.sop
@ [trusted_compilation] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Trusted_Compilation_Profile.sop
@ [tool_checkpoint] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Llama_CPP_Tool_Reflection_Probe.sop

& [RuntimeIdentity] is a separated experimental sidecar
  + [host] is the verified SSH alias evo-x2 at the currently observed 192.168.1.19
  + [Needle_2] is an untrusted learned selector and typed argument extractor
  + [Cantor] is the deterministic contract, digest, query, and proof authority
  + [llama_cpp] is the unmodified provider at loopback http://127.0.0.1:8081
  + [controller] is a bounded local process outside both model engines
  + [release_grade] is effectless_experimental_fixture_only
  - never: call Needle 2 the trust kernel, semantic authority, or source of truth
  - never: represent a sidecar checkpoint loop as one literal shared transformer forward pass

& [AttentionProcedureContract] is a closed content-addressed record
  + procedure_id is a stable namespaced identifier
  + version is an exact profile version
  + description declares the activation use case presented to Needle 2
  + input_schema is one closed JSON Schema subset supported by Needle 2
  + attention_template is the exact provider-visible instruction projection
  + cantor_query_template is absent or one bounded query request template
  + allowed_effects is an empty array in profile 0.1
  + source_ref identifies the governing experimental SOP contract
  + source_sha256 binds the exact source bytes
  + procedure_digest is SHA-256 over the normalized machine contract excluding procedure_digest
  = must: reject duplicate identity, duplicate tool name, unknown field, unsupported schema feature, digest mismatch, missing source, or source digest mismatch
  = must: rebuild the active registry atomically from a completely verified set

& [ProcedureHashing] distinguishes authority from acceleration
  + [authority_hash] is the recomputed procedure_digest bound to source_sha256 and exact normalized contract
  + [catalogue_digest] is SHA-256 over ordered procedure identities and digests
  + [Needle_tool_index] is an optional model-owned retrieval cache keyed by tool schemas and model fingerprint
  + [Needle_confidence] is an advisory routing signal
  = must: verify authority_hash and catalogue_digest in ordinary code before every selected invocation
  - never: treat Needle embeddings, confidence, learned weights, or tool-index similarity as signature, authorization, or proof

& [NeedleBoundary] is constrained
  + [package] is cactus-needle version 2.0.6 pinned for the first experiment
  + [model] is Cactus-Compute Needle 2 obtained through the package's documented engine path
  + [task] is choose zero or one registered attention procedure and extract its arguments
  + [grammar] is generated from the verified selected tool schema
  + [threshold] is explicit in configuration and any below-threshold call escalates without execution
  + [off_topic] is an empty call and produces an explicit no_procedure disposition
  + [continuation] may receive a pure tool result but does not acquire authority from that result

& [CantorBoundary] uses the real query protocol
  + [executable] is a pinned SHA-256 of cantor.exe built from the current repository
  + [environment] is one generated test-only signed environment with its exact digest recorded
  + [operation] is read-only query or inspect only
  + [result] must pass the existing caller verification boundary before provider projection
  + [authority] remains test_fixture_only until separately commissioned keys and corpus are installed
  = must: preserve Cantor faults, omissions, ambiguity, proof, quotes, and result digest
  - never: translate refusal, partial result, unknown state, or transport failure into assent

& [LlamaCPPBoundary] remains provider-only
  + [server] is the existing Vulkan llama-server on EVO-X2 loopback port 8081
  + [model] is the currently pinned Qwen3.5 0.8B validation model for profile 0.1
  + [input] is the user stimulus plus one verified minimal attention frame
  + [return_pass] omits all tools after a procedure result has been supplied
  + [output] is advisory natural-language articulation and never a Cantor receipt
  - never: expose llama-server beyond loopback
  - never: modify llama.cpp, its model, or the existing sop-agent service in profile 0.1

& [RuntimeCycle] is exact and bounded
  * load configuration and pin package, model, llama-server, Cantor executable, environment, and registry identities
  * verify every procedure source and machine digest before creating the Needle catalogue
  * accept one bounded UTF-8 stimulus
  * ask Needle 2 for zero or one procedure call
  * reject malformed, unknown, low-confidence, unverified, or effectful selection
  * execute the selected pure host operation and any bounded real Cantor query
  * construct one minimal AttentionFrame carrying procedure identity, digest, source, Cantor proof references, returned semantic content, and explicit limitations
  * invoke llama.cpp once without tools to articulate a response from that frame
  * validate nonempty provider output and archive a sanitized immutable run record
  * terminate without a resident agent loop

& [InitialProcedureSet] is deliberately small
  + [resolve_sop_subject] queries Cantor for contextual subject identity, applicable descriptions, constraints, and exact source support
  + [inspect_identity_boundary] asks llama.cpp to compare a supplied proposition against the resolved identities without claiming external truth
  + [review_attention_transition] asks llama.cpp to describe preserved, added, removed, and unresolved frame elements
  = must: each procedure have a distinct activation description and exact source-bound digest
  = must: no procedure possess an external effect

& [DeploymentBoundary] preserves other work
  + [remote_root] is C:\AI\services\cantor-needle-runtime
  + [existing_service] C:\AI\services\sop-agent remains untouched
  + [llama_server] remains the existing process and launch configuration
  + [installation] uses an isolated Python virtual environment and a dedicated run directory
  + [network] permits package and model acquisition only during explicit installation, then inference uses loopback
  + [rollback] stops no shared process and removes or disables only the dedicated cantor-needle-runtime directory after evidence preservation

& [Bounds] are closed
  + one stimulus is at most 16384 UTF-8 bytes
  + one procedure catalogue contains at most 32 contracts
  + one procedure result is at most 262144 UTF-8 bytes
  + one provider completion is at most 1536 tokens
  + one run contains at most one Needle selection, one Cantor query, and one llama.cpp articulation
  + timeout is finite for Needle, Cantor, and llama.cpp stages

& [Faults] are typed
  + dependency_fault is missing or changed Needle, Cantor, environment, or provider dependency
  + registry_fault is malformed, duplicate, unsupported, stale, or digest-invalid procedure content
  + selection_fault is malformed, unknown, ambiguous, effectful, or below-threshold Needle output
  + cantor_fault is nonzero exit, invalid response, failed verification, refusal, or unresolved result
  + provider_fault is unavailable, timeout, malformed response, or empty articulation
  + evidence_fault is incomplete, noncanonical, unbounded, or failed run-record publication
  = must: no fault continues into a later stage as success

& [Acceptance] is measurable
  + [ENAR-001] EVO-X2 resolves through the verified SSH alias and the llama.cpp health endpoint is healthy
  + [ENAR-002] Needle 2 package, engine, model identity, and hashes or package records are captured
  + [ENAR-003] three procedure contracts load only after exact source and procedure digest verification
  + [ENAR-004] the same verified registry produces the same catalogue digest repeatedly
  + [ENAR-005] Needle selects resolve_sop_subject with schema-valid arguments for one positive fixture
  + [ENAR-006] off-topic, low-confidence, unknown, changed, and digest-invalid cases never execute a procedure
  + [ENAR-007] the selected procedure invokes the real Cantor read-only query protocol and preserves its proof-bearing result
  + [ENAR-008] llama.cpp receives the verified AttentionFrame without a tool catalogue and returns a nonempty articulation
  + [ENAR-009] the run record distinguishes user input, learned selection, deterministic verification, Cantor result, provider output, and authority limitations
  + [ENAR-010] the existing sop-agent files, llama-server command line, model file, and endpoint remain unchanged
  + [ENAR-011] no external semantic effect is performed
  + [ENAR-012] repeat and negative fixtures are executable through one documented command

& [SJSProcessingTrace] records the seven-fold convergence
  + [fold_1_subject] is a kernel-sized learned selector for content-addressed SOP attention procedures
  + [fold_2_boundary] separates Needle proposal, Cantor authority, llama.cpp articulation, and Narrative personalization
  + [fold_3_data] is procedure contract, source digest, procedure digest, catalogue digest, selection, AttentionFrame, Cantor result, provider output, and run evidence
  + [fold_4_interface] is one CLI stimulus with machine-readable run output and immutable evidence directory
  + [fold_5_security] is loopback provider, empty effect set, exact hashes, confidence escalation, bounded inputs, and fail-closed stages
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is dependency substitution, routing error, digest drift, authority laundering, prompt injection, provider tool looping, and evidence loss
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is one experimental one-shot runtime on EVO-X2 without shared inference, personality learning, effects, llama.cpp modification, or production promotion

& [Signature] is bounded implementation authority
  + [satisfaction_protocol_uuid] is ad10f10f-d506-48ef-a805-f8b0a133766c
  + [signature_uuid] is 093a27d0-2053-4397-b8b9-11c9a6d4733f
  + [source_manifest_sha256] is 35F802A335860C6C97D4C5F004DA9C351078B2FCAA96DB0EE2ABF94F7F1231B9
  + [authority_scope] is the dedicated effectless EVO-X2 Needle 2 attention-procedure experiment, fixtures, deployment scripts, tests, documentation, evidence, and rollback only
  + [invalidation] is changed source, widened effects, unverified procedure, absent Cantor proof, changed shared service, exposed provider, unbounded input, hidden authority, production claim, or profile drift
